<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ban Chao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">32–102</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ban Chao was a general of the Eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/han-dynasty">Han dynasty</a> who brought the city-states of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim Basin</a> back under Chinese control. From the 70s CE he used Shule (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashgar">Kashgar</a>) as a base, subduing kingdoms such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karashahr">Karasahr</a> in 94, and served as Protector General of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-regions">Western Regions</a> from 91. In 97 he sent his envoy Gan Ying westwards towards the Roman world. He was the brother of the historians Ban Gu and Ban Zhao.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ban-chao.jpg" alt="Ban Chao" width="320" height="683" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E6%B1%89%E7%8F%AD%E8%B6%85%E7%AB%8B%E5%83%8F.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
